 to tell the story of  how they met chasing dreams in our  hearts  she said they knew from the start that  they wanted to live and work together  but there were some differences at first  yeah when I first met Christine she's  very frank because I'm joke is this a  German finger but that's interesting  because British people tend to be a bit  more diplomatic about things and then  let something get to a point where they  should have discussed it much earlier  and I think and then it becomes a big  problem whereas Christine just puts me  down all the time and I get used to it  like some of the sinister element  doesn't they've made a name for  themselves in the art world in London  gallery owner Sarah long is an admirer  we've had our young British artists like  Damien Hirst and you know sarah lucas  and they're sort of ironical cynical  reaction to life and here's the  Maguire's with this sort of rather  childlike approach which is very  refreshing their work is also lucrative  these light installations such as the  miniature fairy in a preserving jar can  fetch over 4,000 euros in London and New  York in the real world Kristen and David  McGuire sometimes find it hard to stop  working we had a strict policy of like  not talking about work after six o'clock  for a week we did it I think we've got  two weeks but on the other hand it's  great we've been invited all around the  world and it's just us traveling with  each other which is really really nice  the couple combined the traditional  fairy tale with modern technology to  create a magical world of light and  shadows and finally the Portuguese  island of Madeira lies about seven  hundred and thirty kilometers off the  coast of Morocco and so it enjoys very  moderate temperatures all year round on  the name of its capital city funchal  comes from the portuguese word for  fennel which sailors found growing there  when they discovered the island way back  in the early 15th century while today  it's an oasis of rich 